[00:11.24] (Winwood/Capaldi)
[01:12.80] As time begins to burn itself upon me
[01:25.04] And the days are growing very short
[01:37.52] People try their hardest to reject me
[01:46.76] But in a way, their conscience won't be caught
[01:57.70] Something's happening to me day by day
[02:02.18] My pebble on the beach is getting washed away
[02:10.98] I've given everything that was mine to give
[02:16.38] And now I'll turn around and find that there's no time to live
[02:51.48] So often I have seen that big wheel of fortune
[02:58.10] Spinning for the man who holds the ace
[03:15.80] There's many who would change their places for him
[03:26.56] But none of them have ever seen his lonely face
